  "narrative": {
    "intro": "SDV Office Systems has $265M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. SDV Office Systems received 1,610 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $164K, and obligations are up 20.2% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer, obligating $248M, followed by the Department of Defense with $16.3M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $172K. Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing is the largest market for SDV Office Systems, accounting for $194M in obligations. Other notable markets include Showcase, Partition, Shelving, and Locker Manufacturing at $43.5M and Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $16M. Historical obligations show year-to-year variability: FY21 $59.7M, FY22 $123M, FY23 $62.4M, FY24 $53M, and FY25 $220M. The data are contract obligations except where tables are labeled as award values. This profile highlights where SDV Office Systems derives federal revenue and which product markets and agencies currently drive the bulk of its FY2026 to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are SDV Office Systems' biggest buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $248M. The Department of Defense obligated $16.3M. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $172K. The Department of the Interior obligated $0."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What products and markets drive SDV Office Systems' federal sales?",
        "body": "Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing is the largest market, with $194M in obligations. Showcase, Partition, Shelving, and Locker Manufacturing follows with $43.5M, and Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers accounts for $16M. Smaller markets include Office Furniture (except Wood) Manufacturing at $4.9M and Electromedical and Electrotherapeutic Apparatus Manufacturing at $2.8M."
      }
    ]
  },
